1
00:06:16,666 --> 00:06:22,666
I shot my wife... prove it.

2
00:12:33,333 --> 00:12:39,333
Fracture is a thriller film directed by Gregory Hoblit.

3
00:18:50,000 --> 00:18:56,000
A husband is on trial for the attempted murder of his wife, in what is seemingly an
open/shut case for the ambitious district attorney trying to put him away.

4
00:25:06,666 --> 00:25:12,666
However, there are surprises for both around every corner, and, as a suspenseful game of
cat-and-mouse is played out, each must manipulate and outwit the other.

5
00:31:23,333 --> 00:31:29,333
Theodore Crawford, played by Anthony Hopkins.

6
00:37:40,000 --> 00:37:46,000
William Beachum, played by Ryan Gosling.

7
00:43:56,666 --> 00:44:02,666
Joe Lobruto, played by David Strathairn.

8
00:50:13,333 --> 00:50:19,333
Nikki Gardner, played by Rosamund Pike.

9
00:56:30,000 --> 00:56:36,000
Jennifer Crawford, played by Embeth Davidtz.

10
01:02:46,666 --> 01:02:52,666
Lt. Rob Nunally, played by Billy Burke.

11
01:09:03,333 --> 01:09:09,333
Fracture is a 2007 legal crime psychological thriller film directed by
Gregory Hoblit and written by Daniel Pyne and Glenn Gers.

12
01:15:20,000 --> 01:15:26,000
Starring Anthony Hopkins and Ryan Gosling, it follows a man (Hopkins) who shoots his unfaithful wife
and then engages in a battle of wits with a young assistant district attorney (Gosling).

13
01:21:36,666 --> 01:21:42,666
The supporting cast includes David Strathairn, Rosamund Pike, Embeth
Davidtz, Billy Burke, Cliff Curtis, Fiona Shaw, and Bob Gunton.

14
01:27:53,333 --> 01:27:59,333
Upon its premiere on April 20, 2007, the film received generally positive reviews from critics, who praised its performances
(particularly those of Hopkins and Gosling), style, and tension, though some criticized the plot as implausible.

15
01:34:10,000 --> 01:34:16,000
It was a box office success, earning $92 million against a $10 million budget.

16
01:40:26,666 --> 01:40:32,666
The film explores themes of perfect crime, prosecution, legal thriller.

17
01:46:43,333 --> 01:46:49,333
The tone is intense.
